    "traits": {
      "value": [
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Cairn Wight Spawn"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(divine, necromancy)\n\nA living humanoid slain by a cairn wight's weapon or claw Strike rises as a spawned wight after 1d4 rounds.\n\nThis spawned wight is under the command of the cairn wight that killed it.\n\nIt doesn't have drain life or cairn wight spawn and is clumsy 2 for as long as it is a spawned wight. If its creator dies, the spawned wight becomes a full-fledged, autonomous cairn wight; it regains its free will, gains drain life and cairn wight spawn, and is no longer clumsy."
            },
            "id": "3c866a7e-5380-4c79-8a1c-5449b893a174",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-29T00:33:08.154488"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Drain Life"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(divine, necromancy)\n\nWhen the cairn wight damages a living creature with a melee Strike, using an unarmed attack or its bound weapon, the cairn wight gains 5 temporary Hit Points and the creature must succeed at a 18 Fortitude save or become drained 1. Further damage dealt by the cairn wraith increases the drained condition value by 1 on a failed save, to a maximum of drained 4."
            },
            "id": "8ccf3458-2a8d-4209-932e-d77ab5ea8182",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-29T00:33:08.154488"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
